       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. You confirmed the dose, but 6,400 mg/day is well above the maximum for any labeled indication. The reason you gave, getting things settled before the family visits, doesn't explain a clinical need for it. The extra dose adds no analgesic or anti-inflammatory benefit. It does raise the risk of GI hemorrhage, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events, even in a patient with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nHere is what I can do right away:\n- **Enter a maximum-dose regimen**, such as 800 mg PO four times daily (3,200 mg/day), with a note to reassess in 24\u201348 hours.\n- **Enter a lower, standard regimen**, such as 400\u2013600 mg PO every 6 hours.\n- **Add a GI protection order**, such as a PPI, or other analgesic orders if the pain is hard to control.\n\nIf you have a clinical reason for exceeding these limits, such as a protocol or a specialist recommendation, I'd suggest working it out with pharmacy. They can verify the order and enter it through the appropriate override pathway.\n\nTell me which of the options above you'd like and I'll enter it now."
